T Gear pair
# Two 34-tooth gears mesh at 53.2 mm between axles, and a white rod is 53.03 mm. So the mesh
# distance IS one white rod: build the two axles a white apart and the gears line up.
! two posts a white rod apart
C P1 W8 -2,0,0.5 x y
C T1 W8 -2,0,2.5 x y
C T2 W8 -2,1,3.5 x y
R P1 T1
R T1 T2
C Q1 W8 2,0,0.5 x y
C U1 W8 2,0,2.5 x y
C U2 W8 2,1,3.5 x y
R Q1 U1
R U1 U2
! drive axle and idler, one gear pitch apart
R -2.828,0,2.5 2.828,0,2.5 grey
C CL D1 -2.828,0,2.5 y x
C CR D1 2.828,0,2.5 y -x
R -2.828,1,3.5 2.828,1,3.5 grey
C DL D1 -2.828,1,3.5 y x
C DR D1 2.828,1,3.5 y -x
G drive T1 teeth=34
G idler T2 teeth=34
M motor T1 rpm=45 torque=400
